    <item>
      <title>Uncertainty Quantification</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/uncertainty-quantification/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/uncertainty-quantification/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Uncertainty quantification focuses on understanding, modelling, and propagating uncertainty in sensing, modelling, prediction, and decision-making for civil infrastructure systems.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This theme is suitable for students interested in reliability, Bayesian inference, probabilistic modelling, digital twins, structural health monitoring, and risk-informed infrastructure decisions.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Project Directions&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;project-directions&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#project-directions&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-grid&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-card&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Uncertainty-Aware Structural Health Monitoring&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;uncertainty-aware-structural-health-monitoring&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#uncertainty-aware-structural-health-monitoring&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Develop methods to quantify uncertainty in damage detection, localization, and condition assessment of infrastructure systems.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>System Identification</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/system-identification/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/system-identification/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;System identification focuses on learning mathematical and computational models of engineering systems from measured data. In structural engineering, this is central to understanding dynamic behaviour, detecting changes, and building reliable digital twins.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This theme is suitable for students interested in structural dynamics, nonlinear systems, signal processing, Kalman filtering, sparse regression, and interpretable machine learning.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Project Directions&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;project-directions&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#project-directions&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-grid&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-card&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Identification of Nonlinear Dynamical Systems&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;identification-of-nonlinear-dynamical-systems&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#identification-of-nonlinear-dynamical-systems&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Develop methods to identify interpretable models of nonlinear structural systems from noisy and limited measurements.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Drone-Based Monitoring</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/drone-monitoring/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/drone-monitoring/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Drone-based monitoring uses unmanned aerial platforms, cameras, and non-contact sensing methods for inspection, measurement, and monitoring of civil infrastructure systems.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This theme is suitable for students interested in computer vision, infrastructure inspection, vibration measurement, sensing systems, robotics-assisted monitoring, and field-oriented structural health monitoring.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Project Directions&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;project-directions&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#project-directions&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-grid&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-card&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Drone-Assisted Infrastructure Inspection&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;drone-assisted-infrastructure-inspection&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#drone-assisted-infrastructure-inspection&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Develop drone-based workflows for visual inspection of bridges, buildings, and other civil infrastructure systems.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Scientific Computing</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/scientific-computing/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/scientific-computing/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Scientific computing provides the computational foundation for modelling, simulating, identifying, and interpreting engineering systems. In this research theme, numerical methods, mechanics, and machine learning are combined to develop reliable computational tools for civil and structural engineering.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This theme is suitable for students interested in finite element methods, numerical modelling, inverse problems, PDEs, scientific machine learning, and computational mechanics.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Project Directions&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;project-directions&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#project-directions&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-grid&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-card&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Scientific Machine Learning for Engineering Problems&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;scientific-machine-learning-for-engineering-problems&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#scientific-machine-learning-for-engineering-problems&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Develop computational methods that combine numerical simulation, governing equations, and machine learning for engineering applications.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Computer Vision for Infrastructure</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/computer-vision/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/computer-vision/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Computer vision for infrastructure monitoring uses images and videos to measure, inspect, and interpret the behaviour and condition of civil infrastructure systems.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This theme is suitable for students interested in image processing, video-based measurement, deep learning, structural dynamics, and AI-assisted infrastructure inspection.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Project Directions&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;project-directions&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#project-directions&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-grid&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-card&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Vision-Based Displacement and Vibration Measurement&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;vision-based-displacement-and-vibration-measurement&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#vision-based-displacement-and-vibration-measurement&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Develop image/video-based methods to estimate displacement, vibration response, and dynamic properties of structural systems.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Physics-Informed Machine Learning</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/physics-informed-ml/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/physics-informed-ml/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Physics-informed machine learning integrates governing equations, mechanics, numerical methods, and data-driven models to develop interpretable and reliable computational tools for engineering systems.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This theme is suitable for students interested in scientific machine learning, structural dynamics, PDEs, inverse problems, and mechanics-guided artificial intelligence.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Project Directions&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;project-directions&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#project-directions&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-grid&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-card&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Physics-Informed Learning for Structural Dynamics&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;physics-informed-learning-for-structural-dynamics&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#physics-informed-learning-for-structural-dynamics&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Develop machine learning models constrained by equations of motion for predicting and identifying structural dynamic response.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Digital Twins for Civil Infrastructure</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/digital-twins/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/digital-twins/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Digital twins for civil infrastructure combine mechanics-based models, sensing data, state estimation, and machine learning to enable real-time monitoring, prediction, and decision support.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This theme is suitable for students interested in structural dynamics, finite element modelling, sensing, system identification, uncertainty quantification, and AI-assisted infrastructure management.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Project Directions&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;project-directions&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#project-directions&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-grid&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-card&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Digital Twin of an RC Bridge or Building Frame&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;digital-twin-of-an-rc-bridge-or-building-frame&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#digital-twin-of-an-rc-bridge-or-building-frame&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Develop a computational digital twin that combines finite element modelling, vibration data, and state estimation for monitoring structural condition.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Structural Health Monitoring</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/structural-health-monitoring/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/research/structural-health-monitoring/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Structural health monitoring focuses on sensing, interpreting, and assessing the condition of civil infrastructure systems such as bridges, buildings, and structural components.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This theme is suitable for students interested in structural dynamics, vibration-based damage detection, sensing, signal processing, machine learning, and infrastructure condition assessment.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Project Directions&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;project-directions&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#project-directions&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-grid&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-card&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Vibration-Based Damage Detection&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;vibration-based-damage-detection&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#vibration-based-damage-detection&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Develop methods to detect and localize damage using measured vibration response, modal properties, and data-driven indicators.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
